page('06 | Handover package','NDJSON structure and integrity validation','Preserve exact source bytes before parsing or transformation.',
 table(['Line type','Current contract'],[
 ['header','type=header; schema=NUERS-portability-1; merchant_id; exported_at; descriptive note. exported_at is not an engine commit marker.'],['record','type=record; table; record object. The row fields depend on the current database schema and the allowlist.'],['manifest','type=manifest; tables mapping each table to records and sha256; manifest_sha256. This is the terminal completion record.']],[.23,.77]),
 h('Validation sequence'),
 bullets(
 'Save the original byte stream securely. Require a valid header and terminal manifest; reject truncated, malformed or unexpected trailing content.',
 'For each table, count its record lines and compute SHA-256 over those exact emitted record-line bytes including the terminating LF. Do not parse and reserialize first.',
 'Compare per-table counts/hashes with the manifest; reject missing, duplicate or unexpected required datasets after applying the approved scope.',
 'The manifest hash is computed over PHP JSON serialization of the tables object with its original ordering/encoding. Cross-language verification must reproduce those exact bytes; ordinary reformatting can change the hash.',
 'Check every decryption_error and hash_verified flag. Validate relationship and financial control totals independently of byte hashes.'),
 note('A matching hash shows byte consistency against that manifest. It does not establish who produced it, whether the source query was complete, or whether the destination interpreted the records correctly. Keep transport authentication and business reconciliation as separate controls.'))

